.TH "libnvmf_context_apply_params" 9 "libnvmf_context_apply_params" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_context_apply_params \- apply a parameter set to a connect context.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_context_apply_params
.BI "(struct libnvmf_context *fctx "  ","
.BI "const struct libnvmf_params *params "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "fctx" 12
fabrics context to update
.IP "params" 12
a resolved parameter set
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Applies every set key via its typed setter. An unset key is left
untouched, and an explicit reset (empty string) is skipped, since
\fIfctx\fP already carries the kernel default either way.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, -EINVAL if \fIfctx\fP or \fIparams\fP is NULL.
